     \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\" | \"no_match\",\r\n50:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID, or empty string if no_match)\",\r\n51:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation for review/no_match, empty string for match)\"\r\n52:     }\r\n53:   ]\r\n54: }\r\n55: \r\n56: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\r\n57: - MANDATORY: You MUST return a result item for EVERY SINGLE input case_id. If the input contains N cases, \"results\" MUST contain exactly N items.\r\n58: - NEVER omit any case_id under any circumstances!\r\n59: - For each case_id:\r\n60:   * \"status\": \"match\" (if there is a valid match, specify candidate item_id, empty reason)\r\n61:   * \"status\": \"review\" (if same drug & strength but different dosage form, specify candidate item_id and Arabic reason)\r\n62:   * \"status\": \"no_match\" (if strength conflict, generic alternative, different brand, or no valid match; item_id is \"\", with Arabic reason)\r\n63: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\r\n64: \"\"\"\r\n65: \r\n66: def norm_num(s: str) -> str:\r\n67:     s = str(s)\r\n68:     for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩', '0123456789'):\r\n69:         s = s.replace(e, w)\r\n70:     return s\r\n71: \r\n72: def get_strength_pattern(text: str) -> str | None:\r\n73:     text = norm_num(text.lower())\r\n74:     m = re.search(r'(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(مجم|مج|جم|جرام|gm|mg|mcg|مكجم)', text)\r\n75:     if m:\r\n76:         val = m.group(1)\r\n77:         unit = m.group(2)\r\n78:         if unit in ['جم', 'جرام', 'gm']:\r\n79:             try:\r\n80:                 val = str(float(val) * 1000)\r\n81:             except:\r\n82:                 pass\r\n83:         return val\r\n84:     m2 = re.search(r'\\b(1000|875|625|500|400|300|250|200|150|125|100|80|75|50|40|25|20|15|10|5|2.5|1)\\b', text)\r\n85:     if m2:\r\n86:         return m2.group(1)\r\n87:     if 'ربع' in text or '25.' in text:\r\n88:         return '0.25'\r\n89:     if 'نص' in text or 'نصف' in text or '.5' in text or '0.5' in text:\r\n90:         return '0.5'\r\n91:     return None\r\n92: \r\n93: def has_co(text: str) -> bool:\r\n94:     t = text.lower()\r\n95:     return bool(re.search(r'(?:^|[^\\w])(كو|بلس|بلاس|كومب|co|plus|comp)(?:[^\\w]|$)|كواقراص|كوأقراص|بلساقراص|بلسكبسول', t))\r\n96: \r\n97: def are_forms_identical(form1: str | None, form2: str | None) -> bool:\r\n98:     if not form1 or not form2:\r\n99:         return True\r\n100:     if form1 == form2:\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
